      "message": "fix(ui): browser tree rows read on the light panel\n\negui keeps a dark and a light style and follows the OS appearance; the\ntheme was written only into the slot active at startup, so a light-mode\nMac painted the tree's ink on egui's stock light panel. apply_to now\nfills both slots. Tree rows also stop using the faint (disabled) tier: a\nhidden row and the suffix use the dim tier, and a selected row is all\nbody text so it clears the selection fill.\n\nPinned by tree_ink_tests (both themes, every row ground, both egui slots).\n\nFixes #506\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
